I left out both operations requests. The node's declared capabilities are `LLMClient<[lookup]>` and `DBHandle<'knowledge-base', read>`, and the target has no WASI. The world therefore has no filesystem or HTTP import, and a guest cannot write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or call the metadata service. Adding them would mean granting the node new capabilities in the graph, and the question text would then leave the confined node. That is a decision for the graph owners, not something to do inside the body.

